{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"edits\":[{\"path\":\"summary/text\",\"value_json\":\"白 means “white.” Its early graph is treated as one picture, but its subject is disputed: proposals include a thumb and a cooking or measuring vessel.\"},{\"path\":\"summary/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"formation/text\",\"value_json\":\"Pictographic: the early graph is treated as one picture. A thumb is one proposed subject; another proposal identifies a cooking or measuring vessel, with the middle stroke marking the join between lid and body. Neither identification is settled.\"},{\"path\":\"formation/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref018\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"components/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"The early graph is one pictorial form, not a combination of separate parts. Its referent is disputed: proposals include a thumb and a cooking or measuring vessel.\"},{\"path\":\"components/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref018\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"history/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"The graph is reported to develop from oracle-bone forms through bronze and small-seal forms to regular script. The early referent remains disputed; this proposed sequence does not identify the picture’s subject.\"},{\"path\":\"history/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"history/1/text\",\"value_json\":\"The Shuowen tradition explains the seal form as 入 joined with 二, interpreting 二 as an “yin number.” This is a historical explanation of the graph, not confirmation of its early pictorial origin.\"},{\"path\":\"history/1/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref003\\\",\\\"ref005\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"uncertainties/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"Other proposed subjects include cloth, flame or light, and a face or head. The vessel proposal does not establish the object's ancient name or pronunciation.\"},{\"path\":\"uncertainties/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref004\\\",\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref018\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/period\",\"value_json\":\"Oracle-bone period; individual dated attestations unresolved\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/status\",\"value_json\":\"historical\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"Use for the color word is reported in oracle-bone inscriptions. The first dated example is unresolved, as is whether this was the graph's original referent.\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref019\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/4/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref006\\\",\\\"ref044\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/5/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref006\\\",\\\"ref044\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/limitations/2/text\",\"value_json\":\"The recorded glosses “pure, unblemished” and “bright” are current dictionary senses. A proposed historical chain from white through purity and brightness to clarity and reporting is undated; its transitions are not established here.\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/limitations/2/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref006\\\",\\\"ref038\\\",\\\"ref044\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/overview/text\",\"value_json\":\"白 means “white.” Its early graph is treated as one picture, but the subject is disputed: it may show a thumb or a vessel.\"},{\"path\":\"learner/overview/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"Read the early form as one picture. A thumb and a vessel have both been proposed, but neither identification is settled.\"},{\"path\":\"learner/components/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref017\\\",\\\"ref018\\\",\\\"ref020\\\",\\\"ref037\\\"]\"}]}"}}
